  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). Transitive pair: {剥|は}がす (to peel off).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates resulting state. {剥|は}がれている = 'has peeled off' (state).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {ペンキ}が{剥|は}がれる (paint peels off)\n- {シール}が{剥|は}がれる (sticker comes off)\n- {皮|かわ}が{剥|は}がれる (skin peels)\n\nIDIOM: {化|ば}けの{皮|かわ}が{剥|は}がれる - 'the disguise/mask comes off' - revealing one's true nature.\n\nTRANSITIVE PAIR:\n- {剥|は}がれる (intransitive) - to come off\n- {剥|は}がす (transitive) - to peel off, remove",
